# Asterix & Obelix: Babylon Mission (PPSA30490, Unity 6000.1.5f1 / IL2CPP)
# Reach GAMEPLAY: logo movies -> splash -> title menu -> intro cinematics -> world map ->
# character select -> a platformer level.
#
# NOT the same game as scripts/asterix/reach-gameplay.pad, which drives Asterix & Obelix:
# Slap Them All! (PPSA08576, label game:asterix). That route does nothing here.
#
# THREE phases, and the third one exists because of a measured failure. Triangle is bound to
# different things on different screens:
#
#   Phase A (5-44 s)   Cross only. Logo movies, SPLASH, and the ADVENTURE / OPTIONS title menu.
#
#   Phase B (46-149 s) Triangle, with Cross 3 s behind it. Every cutscene frame draws its Skip
#     prompt bound to TRIANGLE. A Cross-only mash sits through the whole intro: an exploratory run
#     watched Cinematic_A1_Part_1 -> A1_Part_2 -> A2 for 215 s and never left them. Triangle is held
#     1.5 s so a hold-to-skip binding is covered too. Measured cinematic spans: 55-125 s and
#     45-105 s in two runs, so this window covers both with margin at each end.
#
#   Phase C (152 s+)   Cross ONLY, and this is load-bearing. After the map loads, the title shows a
#     character-select screen whose footer reads:
#         (circle) BACK   (cross) START   (square) CUNEIFORM TABLET   (triangle) COSTUMES
#     Triangle there is COSTUMES. A route that keeps mashing Triangle past the cinematics fights its
#     own Cross: whether it ever reaches START becomes timing luck. That is not hypothetical - the
#     first version of this route, which mashed Triangle to the end, reached gameplay in one run and
#     sat on the character-select screen for 495 s in an independent rerun, with IDENTICAL summary
#     numbers (60/60 samples, source-distinct 60, pixel-distinct 58, guest alive, status=ok) because
#     the screen animates. The proof that Triangle was being consumed rather than ignored is that the
#     costume itself changed between t=130 s ("LEGIONARY") and t=600 s ("GOLD").
#
# Progression oracle this was calibrated against - PROSPER_FILELOG=1 names the scene files, and
# Media/levelNN is build-settings scene index NN (76 scenes, 76 files, verified by a byte-level scan
# of globalgamemanagers):
#
#   level0  videoLogos     level1  GlobalManager   level2  PauseManager   level5  MainMenu
#   level38 Cinematic_A1_Part_1    level39 Cinematic_A1_Part_2    level40 Cinematic_A2
#   level6  Loading        level4  Map (incl. character select)   level3  PlatformerLogic
#   level22 World_3_10     level57 World_3_10_Level
#
# Reaching level3 + a World_X_Y/World_X_Y_Level pair is the machine-checkable success condition;
# stopping at level4 is the character-select failure above, and pixel metrics cannot tell them apart.
#
# Bound the run at >= 400 s. Use a private PROSPER_SAVE0: the default save root is one flat directory
# shared by every title on the box (#2734).
